// Foes (game::combat): people-shaped enemies on the NPC rig (npcs.ron looks), each with a
// sword. Ctrl+Shift+J (Cmd+Shift+J) spawns a hollow, Ctrl+Shift+H a shade, a little ahead.
//   ghost:  see-through blue, shimmering, trailing wisps
//   weapon: item it holds (items.ron)
//   damage, cause: a cut that lands (Blunt | Piercing | Chill)
//   reach:  blocks a cut reaches; swing: seconds per swing (wind-up shows how it's coming)
//   walk, run: blocks/s
//   sight:  notices you within this (with a clear line); forget: gives up past this;
//   leash:  never strays further than this from where it began
//   style:  aggression / caution 0..1 (pressing vs circling and backing off),
//           guard 0..1 (chance it blocks your swing), poise (blocks before its guard breaks)
//   ranged: Some((speed, color)): shoots a bolt from up to `reach` away instead of cutting
//           (blocks/s, (r, g, b)); a raised blade stops it
//   role:   Grunt (default) | Shield (blocks from the front, stands before shooters) | Archer (keeps
//           its distance) | Brute (every attack heavy and unblockable) | Skirmisher (circles to your
//           back) | Support (keeps back and mends the others). Every 4th cut of anything that cuts
//           is a heavy one too: slower, flashing red, through any guard. Step out of reach.
//   offhand: item held in the left hand (a shield bearer's shield)
//   Unique shapes come from looks: `scale` and `extras` (boxes on Head / Torso / Hips, as npcs.ron).
// The dungeon foes (sporecaster, rot_brute, mire_skitter) are dungeon-only. Each floor's boss is its theme's
// `warden` (dungeons.ron), the last floor's its `boss` (game::delve::rules::boss_for).
//   boss:   Some((phases: [0.66, 0.33], attacks: [(name, phase, every, wind, kind)])): a phased boss
//           (game::combat::boss). kind: Slam(radius, damage) | Volley(count, damage) |
//           Charge(speed, damage) | Summon(kind, count). A bar shows its health at the top.
